    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1378">

                <pb facs="1229" n="971" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg971"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1766</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgenthau</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-15T10:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 15, 1915, 10 a. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.30 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>665. Your 654. The fifty belligerents [non-combatants?] returned perfectly well
                    and were set free. Philip’s presence at Gallipoli was most useful for hostages
                    and his services invaluable. Out of Gallipoli’s population fifteen thousand have
                    departed leaving about two thousand.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
